    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# 🛠️ Setup Guide  \n**Author:** Ranian Rulona | AKA bit Ransky — AI Automation Developer\n\nFollow the steps below to get this workflow up and running:\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Step 1: Add Your [Vapi](https://vapi.ai/) API Key  \n- Grab your private API key from the Vapi dashboard  \n- In n8n, create a **Generic Credential** using **Bearer Auth**  \n- Attach it to the **Call Lead** and **Get Call Details** HTTP Request nodes\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Step 2: Add the System Prompt to Your Vapi Assistant  \n- Open your Vapi Assistant settings  \n- Copy/paste the system prompt from `prompts/system-prompt-v2.md` in this repo  \n- Add the structured outputs: `call_status`, `urgency`, `scope_of_call`, `system_type`, `unit_quantity`, `preferred_time`\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Step 3: Connect a Phone Number in Vapi  \n- Connect (or purchase) a phone number inside Vapi  \n- In the **Call Lead** HTTP Request node, replace:  \n  - **assistantId** with your own  \n  - **phoneNumberId** with your own\n\n---\n\n### ✅ Step 4: Connect Your Airtable Base  \n- Create a base with two tables — **Contacts** (Name, Phone, Email) and **Service Requests** (Contact, Date, Call Status, Service Type, Urgency, Job Details, Service Location)  \n- In n8n, create an **Airtable Personal Access Token** credential  \n- Point every Airtable node at **your own** base and tables (not the demo base)\n\n---\n\n### 💡 Final Check  \nBefore running, confirm:\n- Vapi API key is present in both required HTTP Request nodes  \n- Assistant ID + Phone Number ID are correctly set in **Call Lead**  \n- Airtable credential + base/table selections point to **your own** Airtable base  \n\nFull reference: `docs/setup-guide.md` | Schema/API details: `docs/api-contracts.md`",
